# Review ownership.
#
# GitHub reads this from the repository root, .github/ or docs/.  A pattern
# further down wins, so the specific entries below override the catch-all.
#
# Left deliberately sparse: an owner who does not review is worse than no
# owner, because it silently blocks. Fill in the areas that have a real
# maintainer and leave the rest to the default.

# Default: anything not claimed below.
*                               @grand-mother/maintainers

# The ROOT schema is a data contract shared across the collaboration, and a
# field name that lands is expensive to change.  See the NUTRIG naming entry
# in docs/source/known_issues.rst for what happens without a single owner.
/grand/dataio/                  @grand-mother/maintainers

# The converters from ZHAireS and CoREAS, maintained by their authors.
/sim2root/                      @grand-mother/maintainers

# Quality machinery: the lint ratchet, the pre-merge check, CI.
/quality/                       @grand-mother/maintainers
/.github/workflows/             @grand-mother/maintainers
/pyproject.toml                 @grand-mother/maintainers
